---
const pillars = [
  {
    title: "PDA vaults",
    body:
      "Agent funds live in Program Derived Address vaults. The Anchor program is the sole signer; agents never hold private keys.",
  },
  {
    title: "On-chain policy enforcement",
    body:
      "Spending limits, destination and program whitelists, and rate limits are stored on-chain and checked atomically on every transaction.",
  },
  {
    title: "x402-native middleware",
    body:
      "Sits between the agent and Solana, routing HTTP 402 payment flows through the vault without server-side changes.",
  },
  {
    title: "Operator dashboard",
    body:
      "Configure policies, monitor transactions in real time, and review a tamper-evident audit trail fed by on-chain events.",
  },
];
---

<section id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="solution-heading">
  <h2 id="solution-heading">How Aegis402 works</h2>
  <p>
    Four layers, one invariant: funds only move through the Anchor program,
    and only if every policy passes. Compromising the off-chain layers cannot
    drain a vault.
  </p>
  <div class="grid">
    {pillars.map((p) => (
      <article class="card">
        <h3>{p.title}</h3>
        <p>{p.body}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
